"textures/gui/server_selection.png","addServer.enterIp","addServer.add","addServer.resourcePack","addServer.hideAddress","addServer.enableCookies","addServer.enableCookies.disabled","addServer.enableCookies.enabled","addServer.hideAddr","addServer.title","addServer.enterName","addServer.SSLWarn1","addServer.SSLWarn2","menu.captureStudio.snipHint","Drag to select area, release to save","options.skinCustomisation.title","options.videoTitle","Render Distance","The render distance controls how far away terrain will be rendered. Shorter distances mean that less terrain will be rendered, improving frame rates.",
"Brightness","Controls the minimum brightness in the world. When increased, darker areas of the world will appear brighter. This does not affect the brightness of already well-lit areas.","Max Framerate","Limits the maximum number of frames per second. This can help reduce battery usage and system load when multi-tasking. If VSync is enabled, this option will be ignored unless it is lower than your display\'s refresh rate.","GUI Scale","Auto","Normal","Large","Sets the maximum scale factor to be used for the user interface. If \"auto\" is used, then the largest scale factor will always be used.",
"Fullscreen","If enabled, the game will display in full-screen (if supported).","VSync","DO NOT DISABLE ON WASM - Due to the WebAssembly frame buffer, your game will stutter. This is a limitation with WASM, not a bug -- ","If enabled, the game\'s frame rate will be synchronized to the monitor\'s refresh rate, making for a generally smoother experience at the expense of overall input latency. This setting might reduce performance if your system is too slow.","View Bobbing","If enabled, the player\'s view will sway and bob when moving around. Players who experience motion sickness while playing can benefit from disabling this.",
"Attack Indicator","Crosshair","Hotbar","Controls where the Attack Indicator is displayed on screen.","3D Anaglyph","If enabled, the game will render in red/cyan 3D anaglyph mode. Requires a resource reload.","If enabled, distance fog is rendered.","Quality","Graphics Quality","Fast","The default graphics quality controls some legacy options and is necessary for mod compatibility. If the options below are left to \"Default\", they will use this setting.","Clouds","The quality level used for rendering clouds in the sky. Even though the options are labeled \"Fast\" and \"Fancy\", the effect on performance is negligible.",
"Smooth Lighting","Minimum","Maximum","Enables the smooth lighting and shading of blocks in the world. This can very slightly increase the amount of time it takes to load or update a chunk, but it doesn\'t affect frame rates.","Particles","Decreased","Minimal","Controls the maximum number of particles which can be present on screen at any one time.","Mipmap Levels","Controls the number of mipmaps which will be used for block model textures. Higher values provide better rendering of blocks in the distance, but could adversely affect performance with resource packs that use many animated textures.",
"The area (in blocks) where biome colors are smoothly blended across. Default is 5x5. Higher values will greatly increase the amount of time it takes to load or update chunks, for diminishing improvements in quality.","Entity Shadows","If enabled, basic shadows will be rendered beneath mobs and other entities.","If enabled, a vignette effect will be applied when the player is in darker areas, which makes the overall image darker and more dramatic.","Cutout Leaves","Controls whether leaves will be rendered as transparent (fancy) or opaque (fast).",
"Controls the distance that weather effects, such as rain and snow, will be rendered.","Chunk Update Mode","If set to \"Deferred\", rendering will never wait for nearby chunk updates to finish, even if they are important. This can greatly improve frame rates in some scenarios, but it may create significant visual lag where blocks take a while to appear or disappear. \"Immediate\" eliminates visual lag by blocking the frame until chunk updates are complete while \"Semi-Immediate\" allows at most one frame of visual lag.",
"If enabled, only the sides of blocks which are facing the camera will be submitted for rendering. This can eliminate a large number of block faces very early in the rendering process, saving memory bandwidth and time on the GPU. Some resource packs may have issues with this option, so try disabling it if you\'re seeing holes in blocks.","If enabled, chunks which are determined to be fully hidden by fog effects will not be rendered, helping to improve performance. The improvement can be more dramatic when fog effects are heavier (such as while underwater), but it may cause undesirable visual artifacts between the sky and fog in some scenarios.",
"Chunk Fix","If enabled, fixes visual glitches at chunk boundaries.","Controls the maximum number of chunk updates per frame.","Chunk Fade Time","Controls the fade-in duration for newly loaded chunks in ticks.","If enabled, only animated textures determined to be visible will be updated. This can provide a significant boost to frame rates on some hardware, especially with heavier resource packs. If you experience issues with some textures not being animated, try disabling this option.","If enabled, entities determined not to be in any visible chunks will be skipped during rendering. This can help improve performance by avoiding the rendering of entities located underground or behind walls.",
"Inactive Max FPS","Limits the maximum frame rate when the game window is inactive.","Controls which fast math implementation to use for sin/cos lookups.\n\nOff: Uses default Java math.\nOptifine: Uses Optifine\'s lookup table.\nLithium: Uses Lithium\'s optimized implementation.","If enabled, Sodium\'s optimized smooth lighting calculations will be used instead of the vanilla implementation. This provides higher quality ambient occlusion with better performance.","If enabled, fluid rendering is handled by Sodium\'s optimized pipeline, improving fluid rendering performance.",
"Advanced","Other","If enabled, the current FPS will be displayed in the corner of the screen.","Show Coords","If enabled, player coordinates will be displayed in the corner of the screen.","FNAW Skins","If enabled, Five Nights at Wilderness character skins are shown.","If enabled, custom item textures from resource packs are used."," chunks","Moody","Bright","Unlimited","Apply","Undo","§l"," *","resourcePack.openFolder","texturepackicon","application/zip","zip","resourcePack.load.loading","Could not load resource pack: {}",
